Morning everyone,

Found an issue during weekend testing. The v2 search endpoint was
returning stale results when the read replica lag exceeded 500ms.
Root cause: we were using eventual consistency reads for the search
index but the freshness requirement is stricter than expected.

Fix: I added a consistency token that forces a primary read when
the client's last-known write is newer than the replica state.
Performance impact is minimal (adds ~3ms per request on cache miss).

Patch is in PR #4518. Carol, can you review?

Also flagging: the Node.js SDK v3.2.0 has a bug in the retry logic
that can cause duplicate POST requests. I filed an issue upstream
and added a workaround in our API gateway (idempotency key check).

- Bob

